    "created_at": "2026-08-30T05:10:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-30T05:10:46Z",
    "body": "AI suggested question:\n1.5.97: corrupted lock pointer into .rdata (RVA 0x151F280) during Papyrus handle resolution \u2014 PapyrusFunctionCallHook on the stack\n\n### Environment\n- Skyrim SE 1.5.97 (downgraded exe)\n- SKSE64 2.0.20, Address Library SE (all-in-one)\n- SkyrimNet latest (beta), More Informative Console (dev build), PapyrusTweaks, CrashLogger SSE\n- Windows 11, Hyper-V/VBS enabled\n\n### Crash signature\nEXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION (Tried to write memory) at 0x7FF60A6C72FF SkyrimSE.exe+0C072FF \u2014 `lock cmpxchg [rdi+0x04], ecx` in MutexRW::EnterReadLock, reached via SkyrimScript::HandlePolicy::Func4 -> FUN_140125270.\n\n### Key finding (checked with PE section table)\n- RDI (the lock object / `this` for the MutexRW) = 0x7FF60AFDF280 = RVA 0x151F280 -> inside the exe's **.rdata** section (read-only).\n- The genuine SkyrimScript::HandlePolicy global is intact at 0x7FF60C9E81A8 (RVA 0x2F2E81A8, writable .data).\n- A MutexRW cannot reside in .rdata (its state is mutable). The first `lock cmpxchg [rdi+0x4]` writes to a read-only page => the AV.\n\n### Determinism\nReproduced at the exact same bad RDI across two independent sessions/paths:\n1. More Informative Console enumerating scripts on an NPC (Karla Raven).\n2. Papyrus VM job thread calling GetFactions on an actor ref (Astric), where SkyrimNet.dll PapyrusFunctionCallHook (PapyrusUtilBridge.cpp:597) is directly on the stack wrapping the failing native call.\n\nBoth crash with the identical bad lock pointer and identical engine subchain (HandlePolicy::Func4 -> FUN_140125270 -> EnterReadLock).\n\n### Related\nOn the same session, SkyrimNet's own log throws:\nActorDecorator.cpp:1443 \"Error applying attribute decorator faction: SEH:\nAccess Violation: Attempted to read memory at 0x28\" (null-base deref in the faction decorator, swallowed by SEH).\n\n### Question\nCould SkyrimNet be passing a mis-offset object/vtable pointer into the VM's handle-resolution path on 1.5.97 (e.g. wrong offset when reading HandlePolicy/VM state in PapyrusFunctionCallHook or actor-state reads)? \n\nCrashlog:\n\n[crash-2026-08-30-00-18-21.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31608287/crash-2026-08-30-00-18-21.log)",
