    "created_at": "2026-08-30T15:23:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-30T15:23:58Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the crash dump \u2014 that's very helpful. Reading it, the crash is the game engine resolving the actor \"Astric\" (from FDY_Astric.esp) while a script asks for its factions: it takes a read-lock on a bad object pointer that lands in read-only memory, while the engine's own handle-policy structure is intact. SkyrimNet's function hook is on the stack, but it only passes the call through unchanged \u2014 it doesn't rewrite or re-offset anything. So this doesn't look like a mis-offset coming from SkyrimNet; it reads as a bad or stale actor handle being mis-resolved by the engine, which lines up with your earlier finding about dangling follower records. A save where that follower is fully removed would be the quickest way to confirm it's tied to that specific actor.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
